# AMD64 thunk export spec -- hid.dll.
#
# From the 2026-08-17 Skyrim Special Edition triage, and the same finding as
# the 2026-08-15 one that added dxgi's and d3d11's: SkyrimSE.exe imports this
# module, Wine provides it as a NATIVE ppc64 builtin, and the loader correctly
# refuses to splice that into a guest call -- reported as c000007b, four times
# over, before the process reaches a single graphics call.  Nothing here is
# hand-written: the export list comes from this module's own .spec.
DLL hid.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

# THE MODULE LOADED AND EXPORTED NOTHING.  Measured before this line existed:
# 0 of 38 eligible exports emitted, all 38 refused as "no declaration found in
# Wine headers", so the generated PE had an empty export table -- it loads, and
# every import of it binds to a missing-import sentinel.  Same class of gap as
# dbghelp's, same one-line fix, and the reason is the same: the HID surface is
# declared in the DDK headers, which the global probe (wine_sig.PROBE_SRC) does
# not include because nothing else needs them.  hidsdi.h carries the HidD_*
# half (device attributes, feature and input reports, the strings a controller
# reports itself by); hidpi.h carries the HidP_* half (the preparsed-data
# parser -- caps, usages, value ranges), and hidsdi.h does not pull it in.
#
# With both, 38 of 38 are emitted and NOTHING is refused: every HidD_/HidP_
# entry point Wine implements is integer/pointer-class in both ABIs.  The six
# names the .spec marks `@ stub` are skipped rather than refused -- Wine has no
# implementation to reach, so a guest that imports HidD_GetConfiguration,
# HidD_GetMsGenreDescriptor, HidD_Hello, HidD_SetConfiguration,
# HidP_GetExtendedAttributes or HidP_UsageListDifference still binds a named
# sentinel and dies naming the symbol, which is the honest answer for an entry
# point that does not exist on this side either.
#
# NO CALLBACKS ANYWHERE IN THIS SURFACE, which is why it is this clean: the HID
# API hands data back through caller-supplied buffers and preparsed-data blobs,
# never through a function pointer native code retains.
PROBE-EXTRA   ddk/hidsdi.h
PROBE-EXTRA   ddk/hidpi.h
